From d385b4695fdff65e98459658ccd87c6309823b67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 14:35:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(auth): repair OAuth callback and email confirmation
 redirect bugs

Google sign-in had no callback route to exchange the OAuth code for a
session, so it silently failed. Email registration also redirected to a
protected page even when Supabase requires email confirmation first,
bouncing users straight back to /auth. Both now resolve correctly, and
the auth page honors ?next= so users return to where they started.

fix(seo): render real content and unique metadata instead of blank shells

/category, /blog and /india-map were shipping near-empty HTML on first
paint because their content only appeared after a client-side fetch -
invisible to crawlers and JS-disabled clients. They now fetch initial
data server-side (category and blog) or render their header/H1 outside
the loading gate (india-map), while keeping client-side interactivity.

Also:
- Add the 7 pages linked from the footer/homepage that 404'd: /careers,
  /press, /mission, /how-to-buy, /sellers, /seller/commission,
  /seller/swadeshi-rank, /seller/terms
- Give ~15 pages that shared the root layout's title/description their
  own unique metadata via per-route layout.tsx files
- noindex the /auth and personalized cart/checkout/seller-dashboard routes
- Fix blog post field mapping (image_url/read_time/state_code -> UI shape)
  shared between the API route and the new server-rendered initial fetch
